{
  "abstract": "Results on the channels K \u2212 p \u2192 \u039b 0 \u03b7 0 , \u039b 0 \u03c0 0 , \u03a3 0 \u03c0 0 , \u039b 0 \u03c0 0 \u03c0 0 and \u03a3 0 \u03c0 0 \u03c0 0 are obtained in a K \u2212 p formation experiment using 1 million photographs taken in a heavy liquid bubble chamber filled with a CF 3 Br\ue5f8C 3 H 8 mixture. The results are compared with hydrogen bubble chamber (HBC) experiments and with experiments having full or partial gamma-ray detection. Our \u039b 0 \u03c0 0 and \u039b 0 + neutral cross section agree with HBC results. Our \u03a3 0 \u03c0 0 cross section does not exhibit a bump at 1670 MeV as previously seen in HBC experiments. Our \u039b 0 \u03c0 0 \u03c0 0 data are dominated by a \u03a3 (1385) \u03c0 0 production. Our \u03a3 0 \u03c0 0 \u03c0 0 data is consistent with the presence of some \u03a3 (1405) \u03c0 0 production.",
